{
  "_readme": [
    "omarchy-launcher categories. Edit freely — the file is watched, so changes show up",
    "the next time you open the launcher (no restart needed).",
    "",
    "HOW THIS IS SHOWN",
    "  The launcher is one column. Every category EXCEPT defaultCategory is drawn as a folder",
    "  row at the top of that column, with its app count and a chevron; opening one swaps the",
    "  rows below the search line for that category's apps, in the same popup. Backspace, ← or",
    "  Esc walks back out. defaultCategory has no folder of its own — its apps are the rest of",
    "  the root list, under a hairline. So: reorder the list here and you reorder the folders.",
    "",
    "Each category takes:",
    "  id            unique key (defaultCategory points at one of these)",
    "  name          label shown on the folder row",
    "  icon          a Material Symbols Rounded icon name (https://fonts.google.com/icons)",
    "  apps          explicit desktop-entry ids, IN THE ORDER YOU WANT THEM SHOWN",
    "  xdgCategories optional: auto-include anything tagged with these freedesktop categories,",
    "                alphabetically, after the explicit ids",
    "  exclude       optional: desktop ids to keep out of an auto-filled category",
    "  configEntry   optional: true pins the \"App List Config\" row to the top of this folder",
    "  all           true = every installed app (used by 'All Apps')",
    "",
    "A desktop id is the .desktop filename without the extension, e.g. org.kde.dolphin.",
    "List them with:  ls /usr/share/applications ~/.local/share/applications",
    "",
    "Every category below was seeded from the apps actually installed on this machine — they",
    "are a starting point, not a guess you have to live with.",
    "",
    "Most of this can be edited without opening a text editor: the \"App List Config\" row at the",
    "top of the System folder opens a window that writes this file (and appearance.json) for you."
  ],
